    "explanation": "Rider — your complaint is that the car was not at the bay, and the record as it stands cannot show that it was: POL-NS-01 limb (b) needs the GPS trace to place the driver inside the 150 m TRANSPORT_HUB arrival radius at or before the arrival event, and limb (c) needs a 300-second dwell measured from the first qualifying in-geofence fix, not from the driver's tap. Neither can be shown, because the only trace for this trip, EV-GPS-09109, is MISSING (issue MISSING_ARTIFACT, weight 0.0). But that absence is not proof the driver was elsewhere. POL-GEN-02 says a missing artifact carries no fact while its absence is itself citable, and POL-NS-02's own drafting note says a trace too sparse to yield three consecutive in-radius fixes is impaired rather than proof of absence. So the arrival and dwell limbs are UNDECIDED, not failed, and an undecided limb supports neither a refund that needs the clause to fail nor a charge that needs it to hold. Your request for the whole SGD 6.00 back (POL-NS-01, POL-NS-02) is therefore not granted on this record, and your alternative argument is the one that governs: escalation holds the fee rather than collecting it.\n\nDriver — your fee is not upheld today either, and the SGD 4.80 you claim is not payable. Your arrived tap at 21:10:20 and the trip record's 5.3-minute wait satisfy POL-NS-01 limb (a) and go to limb (d) (driver-terminated with RIDER_NO_SHOW), and the 320-second arrival-to-cancellation interval clears the 300-second minimum — but that interval is not the GPS-verified in-geofence dwell limb (c) demands, and the trace that would prove both limb (b) and limb (c) does not exist. You are right that POL-NS-04 does not exonerate the rider: you replied 'I am here beside the sign' 15 seconds after the rider's 21:11:30 message, inside the 120-second window, so that clause is out on limb (b). You are right that POL-NS-05's false-arrival test cannot be run without a fix and that no false-arrival finding is made, that the traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-09109-01 is also MISSING (MISSING_ARTIFACT, weight 0.0) so no kerb-restriction accumulation under POL-NS-06(i) or shortfall under POL-NS-06 is established, that the SGD 6.00 line reconciles with fee_schedule.resolution_rule (greater of the TRANSPORT_HUB zone-class fee SGD 6.00 and the RYDE_X tier fee SGD 4.00) so no POL-NS-08(d) fare defect arises, that the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check does not bite (no_show_terminations_30d 1, below 4, and 1/120 = 0.008, below 0.08), and that the POL-NS-09(c) and (d) repeat-abuse triggers do not fire (both counterparty counters 0, no_show_disputes_30d 0). But your compensation claim fails for a prior reason: POL-NS-07 requires POL-NS-01 to be satisfied in full, and it is not. Your own statement — you were at the bay for the full waiting period but the GPS export is unavailable — is evidence, and it corroborates the gap, but it cannot substitute for the test the clause reads. Your conclusion that the charge simply stands (POL-GEN-03 NO_ACTION) is rejected: the arrival limb is undecided and the sole evidence for it is impaired, so nothing on this record supports leaving the fee in place any more than it supports refunding it. (Your claim that mentions prior_no_show_flags does so only to say it is context-only and is not relied on; that is correct and nothing turns on it.)\n\nWhy this escalates rather than being decided: the sole evidence for the deciding fact — the driver's position inside the pickup geofence and how long he held it — is EV-GPS-09109, which is missing and is impaired under POL-NS-08(b) (fewer than six fixes across the waiting window, and no rider_track). POL-NS-08 and POL-NS-09(e) then require the case to go to a human reviewer, and the POL-GEN-02(2) confidence cap is the 0.0 weight of that artifact — below the platform floor of 0.70 stated in POL-NS-09(a) and the policy's confidence_floor. The chat log and trip record are consistent with a genuine wait and with a rider who was present, but because the GPS test admitted no reading at all, those accounts stand in for the test rather than bridging it, and they neither lift the cap nor stop the impaired artifact being the only evidence. The agent version is SYSTEM, so a few passages above didn't render. The escalation is terminal for the automated pipeline: no money moves, and the disputed SGD 6.00 is on hold rather than collected or refunded.\n\nOpen question for the reviewer (POL-NS-09): whether the driver actually entered and held the Woodlands MRT private-hire bay during the waiting window on 2026-09-09, and if so for how long. The reviewer should weigh the driver's statement, the trip record's arrival tap and 5.3-minute wait, and the chat sequence (driver 'I am at the private-hire bay' 21:10:40; rider 'I am at the bay and cannot see your car' 21:11:30; driver 'I am here beside the sign' 21:11:45), and obtain the missing GPS export if it can be recovered. No clause in this category produces a referral on these facts, so the referrals list is empty."
